On Sunday 15 April 2007 18:08, ANDREW PIEKARSKI wrote:
> 3) In any case, they do not enter a cmevla list or dictionary i.e.
> lojbanists need to remember them, note them down individually or whatever.

One can enter a cmevla into jbovlaste. See 
http://jbovlaste.lojban.org/dict/listing.html?type=cmene . There are three 
words for "Hong Kong" in the list, as yet another example of variants.

> 3) Once a new lujvo is approved by the voting process, it becomes official
> - which means (if I understand Pierre) that it enters the official
> baselined lists in gimste, mao'ste and CLL.

Votes determine which definition for a word to use. Whether to use the word at 
all will be decided by the dictionary editor, and I don't know how that will 
happen.

> 3)The lists referred to above seem to be for gismu and cmavo - so where are
> the official lujvo?

There aren't any. There's a list called noralujv.txt, whose contents were 
imported into jbovlaste by the user noralujv, but many of these defs are 
unintelligible.

> 4) Where do I find the CLL list?  I thought the CLL is the same as the
> online Reference Grammar, and there is no word list there.

There isn't a list, but there's at least one discrepancy between the gimste 
and the CLL: {fi'u-} is the rafsi of {cfipu} according to the gimste, but of 
{frinu} according to CLL. ISTR that the BPFK awarded the rafsi to {frinu}, 
but I don't find it.

Pierre


